From 453d0f128fe1006221fea907b183e5e05b025d0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 13:39:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mt-foundation-schema: multitenant pkg + tenant_id columns +
 consolidated migration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Lays the schema foundation the rest of the mt-header series depends on:

* multitenant/ — Manager + Handle + runtime + TenantLoader + plugin
  share-shim (no-cleanup-on-tenant-evict). HeaderName = "x-f5xc-tenant"
  is the canonical identity transport for the header model. Manager is
  built but NOT yet wired into the inference path — see Stage 2 work.

* TableTenant + tenant_id columns on customer, team, virtual_key,
  budget, rate_limit, provider, key, mcp tables. Composite (tenant_id,
  name) unique indexes added where Name was previously globally unique
  on virtual_keys / providers / keys / mcp_clients. The legacy single-
  column Name unique indexes are intentionally NOT dropped here — many
  OSS upsert sites still target them and the resulting "ON CONFLICT
  clause does not match any constraint" failure at startup is worse
  than the constraint. The header-model GORM tenant-scope callback
  (patch2) enforces isolation at the application layer regardless.

* Consolidated migration migrationAddTenantsAndTenantIDColumns:
  1. AutoMigrate the tenants table.
  2. Seed the default tenant with ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING.
  3. AddColumn tenant_id on the eight tables above (default:default).
  4. Backfill any rows the AddColumn default missed.
  5. Create composite indexes for the four name-scoped tables.
  Rollback is intentionally a no-op — undoing this without coordinated
  handler rollback would corrupt the runtime tenant resolver.

* framework/go.mod + transports/go.mod gain require/replace lines for
  the local ./multitenant module.

* transports/Dockerfile.local picks up the multitenant module via
  COPY + go work use so the local k3d image links it into the binary.

* .gitignore picks up go.work.local + go.work.local.sum so the
  per-worktree workspace files don't pollute the working tree on a
  shared-repo developer's box.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
